            <!-- Rich Text Body -->
            <div class="prose max-w-none" x-show="lang === 'zh'">
                <p>做 Meta 广告投放，最容易踩的坑之一是：<strong>素材明明在跑，数据看起来不差，但就是不带量</strong>。</p>
<p>账户里有消耗、有点击、甚至有加购，但 ROI 就是起不来。这种「能跑不能卖」的情况，往往是因为复盘时只看单一指标，没有从多维度交叉判断素材的真实效能。</p>
<p>下面这套清单，拿来就能用。</p>
<hr />
<h2>一、指标交叉分析：先确认素材是否真的「能卖」</h2>
<p>在开始复盘前，先把下面这几个指标组合拿出来看：</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>指标组合</th>
<th>能跑的信号</th>
<th>能卖的信号</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>消耗 + CPM</td>
<td>高消耗 + 高 CPM</td>
<td>高消耗 + 中低 CPM</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>点击 + CTR</td>
<td>高点击 + 高 CTR</td>
<td>点击稳定 + CTR 合理（1%-3%）</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>加购 + 加购率</td>
<td>加购量还行</td>
<td>加购率 &gt; 5%，且和点击率匹配</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>转化 + CPA</td>
<td>有转化</td>
<td>CPA 在目标 LTV 的 1/3 以内</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>检查项</strong>：如果你的素材消耗很高，但加购率低于 3%、CPA 超过目标值的 50%，说明它只是在「跑」，并没有「卖」。</p>
</blockquote>
<hr />
<h2>二、素材分类诊断：把素材归进四个象限</h2>
<p>用消耗量和转化效果两个维度，把素材分成四类：</p>
<h3>象限 1：高消耗 + 高转化 → 主力素材</h3>
<ul>
<li>持续观察，适度放量</li>
<li>备用 2-3 条同风格变体防衰退</li>
</ul>
<h3>象限 2：低消耗 + 高转化 → 潜力素材</h3>
<ul>
<li>排查是否是受众过窄或出价限制</li>
<li>扩大受众测试，看能否提升消耗</li>
</ul>
<h3>象限 3：高消耗 + 低转化 → 「能跑不能卖」</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>立即暂停主力投放</strong></li>
<li>拆解素材元素：钩子、口播节奏、CTA 是否匹配落地页</li>
<li>常见原因：钩子吸引但产品无法兑现承诺、CTA 太硬、落地页跳失率高</li>
</ul>
<h3>象限 4：低消耗 + 低转化 → 边缘素材</h3>
<ul>
<li>小预算跑 3-5 天观察趋势</li>
<li>无提升则直接淘汰</li>
</ul>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>检查项</strong>：每周至少整理一次素材象限分布，如果「象限 3」素材超过 30%，说明素材迭代节奏出了问题。</p>
</blockquote>
<hr />
<h2>三、复盘执行步骤：每条素材过一遍这 5 步</h2>
<h3>Step 1：拉取素材维度的核心数据</h3>
<p>在广告管理工具中，按素材拆分数据，重点看：<br />
- 各素材的消耗、CTR、CPC<br />
- 各素材的加购数、加购率<br />
- 各素材的转化数、CPA</p>
<h3>Step 2：计算「流量转化率」</h3>
<p>公式：<code>转化率 = 转化数 / 点击数</code></p>
<ul>
<li>转化率 &gt; 2%：素材和产品匹配度较高</li>
<li>转化率 1%-2%：可接受，需优化落地页</li>
<li>转化率 &lt; 1%：素材钩子和落地页承诺存在落差</li>
</ul>
<h3>Step 3：检查落地页匹配度</h3>
<p>问自己三个问题：<br />
- 素材第一帧展示的核心卖点，落地页首屏是否呈现？<br />
- 素材承诺的优惠/功能，落地页是否有对应 CTA？<br />
- 素材人群和落地页语言风格是否一致？</p>
<h3>Step 4：分析素材衰减周期</h3>
<p>某工具类 App 团队的经验：</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>测试阶段</th>
<th>生命周期</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>新素材上线</td>
<td>前 3 天 CTR 最高，随后下降</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>稳定期</td>
<td>Day 4-14 是主要产出阶段</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>衰退期</td>
<td>Day 15+ 转化成本上升，需换新素材</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>检查项</strong>：如果某素材在 Day 7 后 CTR 下降超过 20%，即使还在消耗，也该考虑减少预算或上新素材接替。</p>
</blockquote>
<h3>Step 5：记录并沉淀「爆款元素」</h3>
<p>把跑出效果的素材拆解成元素清单：<br />
- 开头 3 秒的钩子是什么（痛点/数字/冲突？）<br />
- 产品的核心卖点展示方式（对比/演示/证言？）<br />
- CTA 的文案和位置<br />
- 背景音乐或配音风格</p>
<hr />
<h2>四、常见问题快速排查</h2>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>现象</th>
<th>可能原因</th>
<th>对应动作</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>消耗快但转化少</td>
<td>受众太宽或素材钩子不精准</td>
<td>缩小受众或更换开头钩子</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>点击高但加购低</td>
<td>素材吸引冲动点击，但产品页不吸引</td>
<td>优化落地页首屏和加载速度</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>CPA 忽高忽低</td>
<td>素材在平台学习期内波动</td>
<td>给素材 5-7 天稳定学习期</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>素材跑几天就衰退</td>
<td>同类素材竞争或受众疲劳</td>
<td>增加变体，保持 3-5 条新素材在测</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<hr />
<h2>小结</h2>
<p>区分「能跑」和「能卖」，核心就三点：</p>
<ol>
<li><strong>指标交叉看</strong>：不要只看消耗和 CTR，用转化率过滤低效素材</li>
<li><strong>四象限定性</strong>：每条素材找到自己的位置，对症下药</li>
<li><strong>流程定期跑</strong>：每周复盘一次，素材生命周期管理到位</li>
</ol>
<p>素材是广告账户的核心。学会在数据里看出门道，才能让预算花得值。</p>
            </div>
            <div class="prose max-w-none" x-show="lang === 'en'" x-cloak>
                <p>One of the biggest pitfalls in Meta advertising: your creative is spending budget, the numbers look decent, but it simply isn't driving conversions.</p>
<p>Having impressions, clicks, even add-to-carts—but no ROI to show for it. This "running but not selling" situation usually happens because your creative review focuses on single metrics instead of cross-dimensional analysis. Here's a checklist you can use immediately.</p>
<hr />
<h2>1. Cross-Metric Analysis: Confirm Whether Your Creative Actually "Sells"</h2>
<p>Before reviewing, check these metric combinations:</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Metric Pair</th>
<th>"Running" Signal</th>
<th>"Selling" Signal</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Spend + CPM</td>
<td>High spend + High CPM</td>
<td>High spend + Low-Medium CPM</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Clicks + CTR</td>
<td>High clicks + High CTR</td>
<td>Stable clicks + Reasonable CTR (1%-3%)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Add-to-Cart + Cart Rate</td>
<td>Decent ATC volume</td>
<td>Cart rate &gt; 5%, aligned with CTR</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Conversions + CPA</td>
<td>Has conversions</td>
<td>CPA within 1/3 of target LTV</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Checklist Item</strong>: If your creative has high spend but cart rate below 3% and CPA exceeding 50% of target, it's "running" but not "selling."</p>
</blockquote>
<hr />
<h2>2. Creative Classification: Map Your Creatives into Four Quadrants</h2>
<p>Use spend volume and conversion performance to classify:</p>
<h3>Quadrant 1: High Spend + High Conversion → Primary Creative</h3>
<ul>
<li>Monitor continuously, scale moderately</li>
<li>Prepare 2-3 style variations to prevent decay</li>
</ul>
<h3>Quadrant 2: Low Spend + High Conversion → Hidden Gem</h3>
<ul>
<li>Check if audience is too narrow or bidding constraints exist</li>
<li>Expand audience testing to increase spend</li>
</ul>
<h3>Quadrant 3: High Spend + Low Conversion → "Running Without Selling"</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Pause from primary placement immediately</strong></li>
<li>Break down creative elements: hook, pacing, CTA match with landing page</li>
<li>Common causes: hook promises something the product can't deliver, CTA too aggressive, high landing page bounce rate</li>
</ul>
<h3>Quadrant 4: Low Spend + Low Conversion → Marginal Creative</h3>
<ul>
<li>Run small budget for 3-5 days to observe trends</li>
<li>Eliminate if no improvement</li>
</ul>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Checklist Item</strong>:整理素材象限分布至少每周一次。如果「象限 3」超过 30%，说明 creative iteration 节奏出问题。</p>
</blockquote>
<hr />
<h2>3. Review Execution: Run Each Creative Through These 5 Steps</h2>
<h3>Step 1: Pull Creative-Level Core Metrics</h3>
<p>In Ads Manager, split data by creative. Focus on:<br />
- Spend, CTR, CPC per creative<br />
- Add-to-cart volume and rate per creative<br />
- Conversion volume and CPA per creative</p>
<h3>Step 2: Calculate "Traffic-to-Conversion Rate"</h3>
<p>Formula: <code>Conversion Rate = Conversions / Clicks</code></p>
<ul>
<li>Rate &gt; 2%: Strong creative-to-product alignment</li>
<li>Rate 1%-2%: Acceptable, optimize landing page</li>
<li>Rate &lt; 1%: Gap between creative hook and landing page promise</li>
</ul>
<h3>Step 3: Check Landing Page Alignment</h3>
<p>Ask yourself:<br />
- Does the core benefit shown in the first frame appear on the landing page above the fold?<br />
- Does the offer/promise in the creative have a matching CTA on the landing page?<br />
- Is the audience targeting and landing page tone consistent?</p>
<h3>Step 4: Analyze Creative Decay Cycle</h3>
<p>Experience from a utility app team:</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Testing Phase</th>
<th>Lifecycle</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>New creative launch</td>
<td>First 3 days highest CTR, then decline</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Stable period</td>
<td>Day 4-14 is main production window</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Decay period</td>
<td>Day 15+ conversion cost rises, requires new creative</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Checklist Item</strong>: If a creative's CTR drops more than 20% after Day 7, even while still spending, consider reducing budget or launching replacements.</p>
</blockquote>
<h3>Step 5: Document and Extract "Winning Elements"</h3>
<p>Break down successful creatives into element inventory:<br />
- First 3-second hook type (pain point / number / conflict?)<br />
- Core product benefit display method (comparison / demo / testimonial?)<br />
- CTA copy and placement<br />
- Background music or voiceover style</p>
<hr />
<h2>4. Common Issues Quick Check</h2>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Symptom</th>
<th>Likely Cause</th>
<th>Action</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Fast spend, few conversions</td>
<td>Audience too broad or creative hook imprecise</td>
<td>Narrow audience or change opening hook</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>High clicks, low cart adds</td>
<td>Creative drives impulse clicks, but product page doesn't convert</td>
<td>Optimize above-the-fold and page load speed</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Erratic CPA</td>
<td>Creative in learning phase fluctuation</td>
<td>Allow 5-7 days stable learning period</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Creative decays within days</td>
<td>Similar creative competition or audience fatigue</td>
<td>Add variations, maintain 3-5 new creatives in testing</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<hr />
<h2>Summary</h2>
<p>Distinguishing "running" from "selling" comes down to three core points:</p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Cross-reference metrics</strong>: Don't just look at spend and CTR—use conversion rate to filter low performers</li>
<li><strong>Use quadrant mapping</strong>: Position each creative in its quadrant and treat accordingly</li>
<li><strong>Run the process regularly</strong>: Review weekly, manage creative lifecycle properly</li>
</ol>
<p>Creative is the heart of your ad account. Learning to read the data correctly is what makes your budget work.</p>
